1
00:00:04,320 --> 00:00:06,160
I cannot approve of this.

2
00:00:06,620 --> 00:00:08,410
You could have
defeated them both,

3
00:00:08,830 --> 00:00:10,910
and yet you allowed
them to escape.

4
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:17,500
It wouldn't be any fun
to kill them right away.

5
00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:23,169
Rabbits should be driven into a corner
and killed at the height of their terror.

6
00:00:23,170 --> 00:00:26,889
But you had to reveal
Berserker's Noble Phantasm.

7
00:00:26,890 --> 00:00:29,890
You should have killed at
least one of them in exchange.

8
00:00:32,810 --> 00:00:34,269
That won't be a problem.

9
00:00:34,270 --> 00:00:37,480
There is no way to counter
Berserker's Noble Phantasm.

10
00:00:38,270 --> 00:00:39,479
Yes.

11
00:00:39,480 --> 00:00:40,899
Noble Phantasm...

12
00:00:40,900 --> 00:00:42,990
Once every three
days, restoration.

13
00:00:43,570 --> 00:00:47,450
Surely you didn't show
mercy to Emiya Shirou.

14
00:00:48,160 --> 00:00:51,200
Of course I did.

15
00:00:51,740 --> 00:00:57,080
I have to make him
suffer in Kiritsugu's place.

16
00:01:10,190 --> 00:01:15,230
In the face of absolute despair

17
00:01:15,530 --> 00:01:19,230
That nearly burned
our hearts away

18
00:01:20,730 --> 00:01:25,780
You still found the
courage to smile

19
00:01:26,030 --> 00:01:30,580
Like you accepted it all

20
00:01:31,380 --> 00:01:33,840
I lost my voice

21
00:01:34,040 --> 00:01:36,460
And the things I wanted to say

22
00:01:36,740 --> 00:01:41,710
But every time I
fell to my knees

23
00:01:42,060 --> 00:01:46,010
I stood up and kept walking

24
00:01:46,280 --> 00:01:51,680
We were looking for
the ideal white future

25
00:01:51,890 --> 00:01:56,910
Our one and only hope

26
00:01:57,240 --> 00:01:59,400
Now I may be left with nothing

27
00:01:59,570 --> 00:02:04,820
But these raging
emotions that have

28
00:02:04,880 --> 00:02:07,920
Nowhere to go

29
00:02:08,170 --> 00:02:13,170
Still, I'll look for a new dawn

30
00:02:13,550 --> 00:02:16,580
With more than one right answer

31
00:02:16,820 --> 00:02:20,410
I won't stop

32
00:02:20,710 --> 00:02:22,440
Until I find it

33
00:02:45,480 --> 00:02:46,780
You're awake?

34
00:02:47,230 --> 00:02:48,400
That's a good sign.

35
00:02:50,570 --> 00:02:53,490
Oh, your injuries seem
to have healed already.

36
00:02:53,491 --> 00:02:55,580
Finding the Will to Fight

37
00:02:53,490 --> 00:02:55,659
T-Tohsaka...

38
00:02:55,660 --> 00:02:57,409
What are you...

39
00:02:57,410 --> 00:02:59,709
Wait, what did I do?

40
00:02:59,710 --> 00:03:02,330
Pick one thing to
be surprised about.

41
00:03:02,920 --> 00:03:03,920
I see.

42
00:03:04,630 --> 00:03:07,840
I passed out, and you
carried me back here.

43
00:03:09,340 --> 00:03:12,049
So you're not as
dumb as you look.

44
00:03:12,050 --> 00:03:14,849
That's very interesting.

45
00:03:14,850 --> 00:03:15,680
Well, goodbye.

46
00:03:15,680 --> 00:03:16,680
Tohsaka...

47
00:03:17,180 --> 00:03:19,600
I should have said
this earlier, but thanks.

48
00:03:21,230 --> 00:03:22,230
Wait.

49
00:03:22,770 --> 00:03:24,979
Why are you thanking me?

50
00:03:24,980 --> 00:03:27,819
Well, you saved me, didn't you?

51
00:03:27,820 --> 00:03:30,649
You shouldn't thank an enemy.

52
00:03:30,650 --> 00:03:33,409
The Holy Grail War
is a fight to the death.

53
00:03:33,410 --> 00:03:36,950
Then why didn't you kill me?

54
00:03:37,780 --> 00:03:40,949
I-I just didn't feel like it!

55
00:03:40,950 --> 00:03:43,460
Attacking someone
in their sleep isn't fair.

56
00:03:44,040 --> 00:03:46,669
So it was a blunder on my part.

57
00:03:46,670 --> 00:03:50,459
I lowered my guard, perhaps
because I'm more powerful.

58
00:03:50,460 --> 00:03:52,969
You could say I have
some emotional flab.

59
00:03:52,970 --> 00:03:55,339
Emotional flab?

60
00:03:55,340 --> 00:03:58,050
Are you saying that you're fat?

61
00:03:59,350 --> 00:04:01,430
You're such a funny boy!

62
00:04:10,150 --> 00:04:13,650
Well, the next time we
meet, it will be as enemies.

63
00:04:14,070 --> 00:04:15,950
So be prepared.

64
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:23,750
Are we finally
going home, Master?

65
00:04:25,040 --> 00:04:27,500
We can't return
empty-handed, can we?

66
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:30,130
I have to make
amends for my blunder.

67
00:04:38,890 --> 00:04:40,510
Where's Saber?

68
00:04:58,370 --> 00:05:00,579
Saber, what are
you doing in here?

69
00:05:00,580 --> 00:05:02,410
I have been resting.

70
00:05:02,950 --> 00:05:06,119
I thought I should at least
get into peak condition.

71
00:05:06,120 --> 00:05:08,539
Shirou, how are your injuries?

72
00:05:08,540 --> 00:05:10,880
Everything's fine.

73
00:05:11,710 --> 00:05:12,800
I'm glad.

74
00:05:13,340 --> 00:05:15,380
I must say, I am impressed.

75
00:05:15,970 --> 00:05:18,890
I did not expect you to
possess self-healing magic.

76
00:05:22,430 --> 00:05:26,940
Shirou, regarding last night,
there is something I feel I must say.

77
00:05:27,770 --> 00:05:31,440
I must ask that you, my Master,
refrain from such actions in the future.

78
00:05:32,190 --> 00:05:34,529
What choice did I have?

79
00:05:34,530 --> 00:05:36,899
You were in danger.

80
00:05:36,900 --> 00:05:41,580
You would place so much confidence
in a Servant you've only just met?

81
00:05:42,030 --> 00:05:44,200
We shook on it, didn't we?

82
00:05:50,790 --> 00:05:54,710
Your words are gratifying
to me as a Servant.

83
00:05:55,630 --> 00:05:56,630
However...

84
00:05:57,840 --> 00:05:59,679
In the future, please
restrain yourself.

85
00:05:59,680 --> 00:06:02,599
I would have you
win the Grail for me.

86
00:06:02,600 --> 00:06:06,179
You want the Holy Grail, too?

87
00:06:06,180 --> 00:06:07,389
Yes.

88
00:06:07,390 --> 00:06:10,060
So that I might
fulfill my own wish.

89
00:06:14,940 --> 00:06:17,030
We Servants are Heroic Spirits.

90
00:06:17,740 --> 00:06:21,569
As a result of that fame, when
we make known our true identities,

91
00:06:21,570 --> 00:06:24,330
we also reveal our weaknesses.

92
00:06:25,490 --> 00:06:29,659
So you go by "Saber"
to hide your real name?

93
00:06:29,660 --> 00:06:31,039
Yes.

94
00:06:31,040 --> 00:06:34,249
The Grail summons
seven Servants,

95
00:06:34,250 --> 00:06:37,669
each selected
based on their class.

96
00:06:37,670 --> 00:06:41,590
Class? Like swordsman or bowman?

97
00:06:41,930 --> 00:06:42,930
Yes.

98
00:06:43,430 --> 00:06:46,769
The Grail prepares
seven vessels in advance

99
00:06:46,770 --> 00:06:51,390
and summons Heroic Spirits from
all eras that match those vessels.

100
00:06:52,310 --> 00:06:54,150
These are the seven classes:

101
00:06:54,810 --> 00:06:57,479
Saber, Lancer,

102
00:06:57,480 --> 00:07:01,109
Archer, Rider, Caster,

103
00:07:01,110 --> 00:07:03,780
Assassin, and Berserker.

104
00:07:04,820 --> 00:07:06,529
I get it.

105
00:07:06,530 --> 00:07:09,619
As a hero, you were
proficient with a sword,

106
00:07:09,620 --> 00:07:11,870
so you were summoned
into the Saber class.

107
00:07:12,330 --> 00:07:16,539
But from a different perspective, that
skill is also the Saber class's drawback.

108
00:07:16,540 --> 00:07:18,249
Drawback?

109
00:07:18,250 --> 00:07:22,509
Say you were faced with an opponent more
skilled than you in close-quarters combat.

110
00:07:22,510 --> 00:07:24,469
What would you do?

111
00:07:24,470 --> 00:07:27,720
Well, if I couldn't
win head-on...

112
00:07:28,970 --> 00:07:31,310
I'd have to resort to a more
underhanded approach.

113
00:07:31,690 --> 00:07:33,399
Exactly.

114
00:07:33,400 --> 00:07:35,810
In addition, we possess what
are called "Noble Phantasms".

115
00:07:36,440 --> 00:07:42,490
Lancer's spear, Archer's bow, and my
sword are all examples of Noble Phantasms.

116
00:07:42,950 --> 00:07:46,159
Noble Phantasms are
Servants' trump cards.

117
00:07:46,160 --> 00:07:50,580
However, a significant amount of
mana is required for their activation.

118
00:07:50,910 --> 00:07:53,920
In other words, you can't
use them all the time?

119
00:07:54,290 --> 00:07:55,709
That is correct.

120
00:07:55,710 --> 00:07:57,851
What's more, a
Servant must call out the

121
00:07:57,863 --> 00:08:00,339
Noble Phantasm's true
name when activating it,

122
00:08:00,340 --> 00:08:04,259
so they run the risk of
revealing their identity.

123
00:08:04,260 --> 00:08:07,760
Oh, so that's why you
make your sword invisible.

124
00:08:08,890 --> 00:08:12,430
Shirou, I have a favor
to ask related to that.

125
00:08:13,230 --> 00:08:15,350
It concerns my true name.

126
00:08:15,810 --> 00:08:18,334
Normally, a Servant
reveals their identity to

127
00:08:18,346 --> 00:08:20,939
their Master so they
can formulate a strategy.

128
00:08:20,940 --> 00:08:24,110
However, you are
unskilled as a mage.

129
00:08:24,490 --> 00:08:28,830
There is a chance that an experienced
mage could read your thoughts.

130
00:08:29,830 --> 00:08:30,830
So I...

131
00:08:31,790 --> 00:08:34,330
So you can't reveal
your name to me.

132
00:08:37,710 --> 00:08:39,039
I understand.

133
00:08:39,040 --> 00:08:43,090
I'll leave your Noble
Phantasm's use to your discretion.

134
00:08:45,180 --> 00:08:47,510
Now that that's settled,
let's have breakfast.

135
00:08:48,760 --> 00:08:51,310
Before I forget, where did
those clothes come from?

136
00:08:51,770 --> 00:08:53,680
Rin gave them to me.

137
00:08:54,680 --> 00:08:58,150
She said that since I cannot
dematerialize, I require ordinary clothes.

138
00:08:58,980 --> 00:09:02,730
So she wears prim and
proper outfits like that...

139
00:09:05,070 --> 00:09:07,660
DO NOT ENTER

140
00:09:10,530 --> 00:09:13,660
It's faint, but I
sense mana residue.

141
00:09:14,290 --> 00:09:17,670
Which means that
was no simple gas leak.

142
00:09:18,250 --> 00:09:20,590
How could they
involve civilians in this?

143
00:09:25,630 --> 00:09:27,259
I'm sorry.

144
00:09:27,260 --> 00:09:29,425
Masters are supposed
to replenish their

145
00:09:29,437 --> 00:09:32,060
Servants, but since I'm
such a novice, I can't.

146
00:09:33,220 --> 00:09:37,060
I can minimize my mana
expenditure by sleeping.

147
00:09:40,190 --> 00:09:41,190
Homurahara Academy

148
00:09:41,191 --> 00:09:42,191
Archery Dojo

149
00:09:43,230 --> 00:09:45,279
Hello, Emiya residence.

150
00:09:45,280 --> 00:09:48,280
Hey, Fujimura here!

151
00:09:48,700 --> 00:09:50,319
Fuji-nee?

152
00:09:50,320 --> 00:09:52,699
What is it? I'm a
little busy right now.

153
00:09:52,700 --> 00:09:55,119
Well, so am I!

154
00:09:55,120 --> 00:09:59,290
I'm giving up my day
off for my students.

155
00:09:59,870 --> 00:10:05,129
Anyway, make me lunch and
bring it to the archery dojo ASAP!

156
00:10:05,130 --> 00:10:06,170
Over!

157
00:10:07,380 --> 00:10:08,380
Huh?

158
00:10:11,890 --> 00:10:13,430
Look, Saber...

159
00:10:13,970 --> 00:10:17,230
Aren't Masters supposed
to avoid attracting attention?

160
00:10:18,140 --> 00:10:20,729
I don't think we'll get a repeat
of last night in broad daylight.

161
00:10:20,730 --> 00:10:23,310
But there is always a
possibility, however small.

162
00:10:23,940 --> 00:10:26,860
It wouldn't be safe to allow
you to walk outside on your own.

163
00:10:33,410 --> 00:10:38,750
Saber, if someone tries to talk to you,
just shake your head without replying.

164
00:10:39,160 --> 00:10:42,380
It'd be best for you to act
like you don't know Japanese.

165
00:10:45,210 --> 00:10:46,210
Saber?

166
00:10:46,710 --> 00:10:48,880
I can sense residual mana.

167
00:10:49,630 --> 00:10:53,759
Something feels off, but it
doesn't seem to pose any danger.

168
00:10:53,760 --> 00:10:56,810
I said it was safe, didn't I?

169
00:11:02,900 --> 00:11:03,900
Hey.

170
00:11:05,150 --> 00:11:07,730
I'm here with
lunch for Fuji-nee.

171
00:11:08,610 --> 00:11:11,110
Would you mind
calling her for me?

172
00:11:16,280 --> 00:11:17,740
Ah, sure.

173
00:11:20,160 --> 00:11:22,499
Boy, am I glad to see you.

174
00:11:22,500 --> 00:11:24,709
You got her lunch?

175
00:11:24,710 --> 00:11:29,129
Fujimura-sensei's been a handful. When
she's hungry, she gets all high-strung.

176
00:11:29,130 --> 00:11:33,509
Why didn't you check first thing in the
morning to see if she'd brought lunch?

177
00:11:33,510 --> 00:11:36,429
Well, I was kinda
worn out myself.

178
00:11:36,430 --> 00:11:39,889
Shinji again? Where is he today?

179
00:11:39,890 --> 00:11:43,519
Playing hooky. I think
he has a new girlfriend.

180
00:11:43,520 --> 00:11:45,059
But anyway, Emiya...

181
00:11:45,060 --> 00:11:47,149
Who was that woman out front?

182
00:11:47,150 --> 00:11:48,870
She was gorgeous. Is
she a friend of yours?

183
00:11:49,320 --> 00:11:52,570
Um, it's kind of complicated.

184
00:11:54,070 --> 00:11:55,070
"Was"?

185
00:12:27,440 --> 00:12:28,940
Kuzuki-sensei!

186
00:12:34,240 --> 00:12:35,240
Emiya?

187
00:12:35,910 --> 00:12:38,199
She's an acquaintance of mine.

188
00:12:38,200 --> 00:12:40,699
She's sort of here to
check out the school.

189
00:12:40,700 --> 00:12:43,370
We've never had a student
from overseas before.

190
00:12:45,670 --> 00:12:48,499
If she enrolled, she'd
be an object of curiosity.

191
00:12:48,500 --> 00:12:51,420
You should look
out for her, Emiya.

192
00:12:52,460 --> 00:12:53,800
Yes, sir.

193
00:12:55,930 --> 00:12:57,590
Incidentally, Emiya...

194
00:13:00,140 --> 00:13:02,680
Outdoor shoes are forbidden
in the school building.

195
00:13:08,150 --> 00:13:11,479
Shirou, about that instructor...

196
00:13:11,480 --> 00:13:13,400
Did you sense something
about Kuzuki-sensei?

197
00:13:13,780 --> 00:13:18,239
Not exactly. At first, he struck
me as being more than he seemed.

198
00:13:18,240 --> 00:13:21,739
But he is not a mage,
nor does he smell of blood.

199
00:13:21,740 --> 00:13:25,289
If Kuzuki-sensei turned out
to be a mage, I'd be shocked.

200
00:13:25,290 --> 00:13:28,040
But what do you mean,
"more than he seemed"?

201
00:13:28,370 --> 00:13:32,379
His breathing was exceedingly
natural and composed.

202
00:13:32,380 --> 00:13:35,049
Frankly, I was quite impressed.

203
00:13:35,050 --> 00:13:36,880
Even his gait was
perfectly efficient.

204
00:13:37,380 --> 00:13:41,220
His pupils must be at ease
with such a man as their teacher.

205
00:13:41,800 --> 00:13:44,059
Shall we proceed
to the next location?

206
00:13:44,060 --> 00:13:47,639
Wait, you want to go
all around the school?

207
00:13:47,640 --> 00:13:50,270
Yes, until I have
ascertained that it is safe.

208
00:13:57,700 --> 00:13:59,159
I'm exhausted.

209
00:13:59,160 --> 00:14:01,029
Huh? Emiya?

210
00:14:01,030 --> 00:14:02,870
You're still at school?

211
00:14:03,410 --> 00:14:04,789
You guys finish already?

212
00:14:04,790 --> 00:14:07,210
Yeah, we're wrapping
up early today.

213
00:14:07,580 --> 00:14:09,580
Ah. Well, keep up the hard work.

214
00:14:13,040 --> 00:14:14,340
Hey, Emiya...

215
00:14:15,800 --> 00:14:18,050
Will you ever come
back to the archery club?

216
00:14:20,760 --> 00:14:24,599
It sounds like Fujimura-sensei
is trying to talk you into it,

217
00:14:24,600 --> 00:14:25,890
but where do you stand?

218
00:14:27,560 --> 00:14:29,230
Well...

219
00:14:29,810 --> 00:14:33,899
I'm thinking of giving it another
shot once I get things sorted out.

220
00:14:33,900 --> 00:14:35,109
You are?

221
00:14:35,110 --> 00:14:36,319
That's a bit surprising.

222
00:14:36,320 --> 00:14:37,440
Surprising?

223
00:14:37,940 --> 00:14:41,279
From the minute you joined,
you were so good it was scary.

224
00:14:41,280 --> 00:14:44,529
But it always seemed like you
weren't interested in hitting the target.

225
00:14:44,530 --> 00:14:47,450
Or maybe you didn't
have the desire to.

226
00:14:47,870 --> 00:14:50,709
I just assumed you quit
because you got bored.

227
00:14:50,710 --> 00:14:54,839
It's like you have no
desire for anything.

228
00:14:54,840 --> 00:14:56,379
Really?

229
00:14:56,380 --> 00:15:00,220
I'm not saying you should be like
Shinji, but why not try to have some fun?

230
00:15:03,180 --> 00:15:04,390
Man...

231
00:15:05,180 --> 00:15:08,519
If a fellow student's worrying
about me, it must be really bad.

232
00:15:08,520 --> 00:15:11,640
I mean, you never laugh, Emiya.

233
00:15:22,360 --> 00:15:24,490
Remember training camp?

234
00:15:25,030 --> 00:15:27,773
When we were all having
fun, you were the only one

235
00:15:27,785 --> 00:15:30,539
who didn't so much as
chuckle at my best material.

236
00:15:30,540 --> 00:15:31,619
Yeah...

237
00:15:31,620 --> 00:15:33,580
I'm still holding a grudge.

238
00:15:34,500 --> 00:15:38,920
Well, I need to drop by the faculty
office, so I'll see you tomorrow.

239
00:15:43,380 --> 00:15:45,140
Mitsuzuri...

240
00:15:58,690 --> 00:16:01,900
That girl's been following us.

241
00:16:02,740 --> 00:16:05,279
Do you know her, Senpai?

242
00:16:05,280 --> 00:16:07,909
Yeah, she's an old
acquaintance of my dad's.

243
00:16:07,910 --> 00:16:10,199
Of Kiritsugu-san's?

244
00:16:10,200 --> 00:16:13,579
She came to visit
Kiritsugu-san, then?

245
00:16:13,580 --> 00:16:15,579
That's right.

246
00:16:15,580 --> 00:16:19,090
She'll be staying at my place
for a while, so be nice to her.

247
00:16:26,510 --> 00:16:27,680
Staying at your place?

248
00:16:28,180 --> 00:16:29,929
You're shacking up with her?

249
00:16:29,930 --> 00:16:31,599
We aren't shacking up.

250
00:16:31,600 --> 00:16:34,770
Saber will only be
staying for a little while.

251
00:16:35,140 --> 00:16:38,019
She's called Saber-san?

252
00:16:38,020 --> 00:16:40,980
Yeah. I'd really appreciate it if you'd
try to be friends with her, Sakura.

253
00:16:42,400 --> 00:16:45,359
Sure, I can do that.

254
00:16:45,360 --> 00:16:46,360
Fujimura-sensei!

255
00:16:46,820 --> 00:16:50,490
Are you giving her your
approval to stay, Fujimura-sensei?

256
00:16:51,790 --> 00:16:54,869
As a teacher, I'd say
it's out of the question,

257
00:16:54,870 --> 00:16:59,000
but I can't turn away a girl who's
come here to see Kiritsugu-san, so...

258
00:17:08,050 --> 00:17:09,549
Sure, why not?

259
00:17:09,550 --> 00:17:11,510
Just think of it as a homestay!

260
00:17:53,850 --> 00:17:56,429
Temperatures are
expected to fall again tonight.

261
00:17:56,430 --> 00:17:59,270
And here I'd pulled out all
the stops for this dinner...

262
00:17:57,100 --> 00:17:59,270
Please exercise
caution when driving.

263
00:17:59,900 --> 00:18:02,610
Sakura didn't
come to help, either.

264
00:18:02,611 --> 00:18:04,119
Up next, we have
the weather report.

265
00:18:04,131 --> 00:18:06,371
Fuji-nee, it's getting late.
Mind walking Sakura home?

266
00:18:06,570 --> 00:18:07,699
Good evening.

267
00:18:07,700 --> 00:18:09,200
- Now for tomorrow's forecast.
- Fuji-nee?

268
00:18:09,203 --> 00:18:13,199
The Japanese islands are under a strong,
wintry pressure-distribution pattern.

269
00:18:13,200 --> 00:18:17,000
It looks like this may bring nasty
weather with a focus on northern Japan.

270
00:18:13,530 --> 00:18:14,950
Hello?

271
00:18:15,750 --> 00:18:18,790
Didn't you hear me,
Fujimura-sensei?

272
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:19,500
Let's take a look at how the
clouds have moved since yesterday.

273
00:18:19,501 --> 00:18:20,879
Sorry, request denied.

274
00:18:20,880 --> 00:18:23,590
I won't be able to walk
Sakura-chan home for a while.

275
00:18:20,880 --> 00:18:24,025
The small clouds that had
formed over the Sea of Japan

276
00:18:24,026 --> 00:18:25,130
Why not?

277
00:18:25,131 --> 00:18:27,510
And northern Japan are moving
to the east, toward the sea.

278
00:18:28,800 --> 00:18:31,390
Because starting today,
I'll be staying here too.

279
00:18:31,760 --> 00:18:32,720
Huh?

280
00:18:32,721 --> 00:18:35,059
Care to join me, Sakura-chan?

281
00:18:35,060 --> 00:18:38,850
I can call your
folks, so don't worry.

282
00:18:39,390 --> 00:18:41,349
Y-Yes! Please!

283
00:18:41,350 --> 00:18:43,309
I can always count on
you, Fujimura-sensei!

284
00:18:43,310 --> 00:18:45,189
E-Eh?

285
00:18:45,190 --> 00:18:48,779
Okay! Let's use the tatami
mat room in the back.

286
00:18:48,780 --> 00:18:50,819
There are lots of
spare mattresses.

287
00:18:50,820 --> 00:18:52,530
You don't mind, do
you, Saber-chan?

288
00:19:56,680 --> 00:19:58,849
What kind of incense is this?

289
00:19:58,850 --> 00:20:00,729
A witch's potion, most likely.

290
00:20:00,730 --> 00:20:03,890
Possibly a poison
meant to destroy love.

291
00:20:04,480 --> 00:20:06,900
In which case, we're
dealing with a woman?

292
00:20:07,690 --> 00:20:11,150
Her resentment must be deep-rooted
for her to still act on it as a Servant.

293
00:20:11,860 --> 00:20:14,660
Enough talk. Let's
open the windows.

294
00:20:21,830 --> 00:20:24,170
The flow is toward
Ryuudou Temple?

295
00:20:24,540 --> 00:20:29,129
Yes, the stolen life force is all
flowing toward the mountains.

296
00:20:29,130 --> 00:20:32,339
The culprit behind the coma
incidents is probably Caster.

297
00:20:32,340 --> 00:20:35,299
A witch inhabiting
Ryuudou Temple, huh?

298
00:20:35,300 --> 00:20:38,100
That means we made
a mistake last night.

299
00:20:38,510 --> 00:20:39,510
A mistake?

300
00:20:39,511 --> 00:20:42,179
Fighting Berserker
to a draw, you mean?

301
00:20:42,180 --> 00:20:44,389
I think that was the
optimal outcome.

302
00:20:44,390 --> 00:20:45,639
I'm not so sure.

303
00:20:45,640 --> 00:20:51,530
If Caster's spread such a wide net,
she must have observed last night's battle.

304
00:20:51,940 --> 00:20:57,280
And yet we tipped our hand while
failing to defeat our opponents.

305
00:20:59,330 --> 00:21:00,530
Perhaps.

306
00:21:01,950 --> 00:21:03,290
We'll track Caster.

307
00:21:03,950 --> 00:21:06,170
You can still sense her, right?

308
00:21:06,620 --> 00:21:09,629
We'll put an end to this before
she can flee to Ryuudou Temple.

309
00:21:09,630 --> 00:21:13,879
I thought your policy was to avoid
things that you know are beyond you.

310
00:21:13,880 --> 00:21:14,880
It still is.

311
00:21:15,010 --> 00:21:17,220
But don't you think
this is a special case?

312
00:21:17,970 --> 00:21:21,260
You won't be satisfied
until you start a fight, huh?

313
00:21:23,220 --> 00:21:28,400
You're ignoring an easily defeated opponent
and going after the most difficult one.

314
00:21:29,100 --> 00:21:30,649
It's fine.

315
00:21:30,650 --> 00:21:33,280
We can take him out
whenever we want.

316
00:21:33,860 --> 00:21:38,280
I'm just choosing to ignore him as
long as he stays hidden at home.

317
00:21:38,860 --> 00:21:41,949
Then what if Emiya
Shirou comes to you,

318
00:21:41,950 --> 00:21:45,290
still choosing to ignore
the fact that he is a Master?

319
00:21:47,920 --> 00:21:49,290
I'll kill him.

320
00:21:49,920 --> 00:21:55,090
I'll show no quarter to anyone
who doesn't understand that.

321
00:22:10,400 --> 00:22:16,539
We didn't understand anything

322
00:22:16,540 --> 00:22:22,709
My left hand groped for
things that vanished to my touch

323
00:22:22,710 --> 00:22:25,709
A moral conflict

324
00:22:25,710 --> 00:22:28,510
stays your hand

325
00:22:28,760 --> 00:22:31,259
and tricks you

326
00:22:31,260 --> 00:22:33,140
out of your future

327
00:22:33,390 --> 00:22:40,059
I don't know how
to protect anyone,

328
00:22:40,060 --> 00:22:45,860
and my ideals might
well be pointless,

329
00:22:46,070 --> 00:22:54,070
but I want to live my life

330
00:22:55,070 --> 00:23:00,079
The past repeats before my eyes

331
00:23:00,080 --> 00:23:07,879
Here I will trust the me
that now stands with you

332
00:23:07,880 --> 00:23:13,969
Until my dream
crumbles and withers,

333
00:23:13,970 --> 00:23:19,599
I hope you will carve
out paradise with me

334
00:23:19,600 --> 00:23:23,310
Fight your fate

335
00:23:26,810 --> 00:23:28,309
Sakura and I have
broken the ice.

336
00:23:28,310 --> 00:23:31,689
I know my brother
better than anyone.

337
00:23:31,690 --> 00:23:33,519
No. I will not give you
the Command Spells.

338
00:23:33,520 --> 00:23:35,689
Just prepare yourself, Shirou!

339
00:23:35,690 --> 00:23:38,045
I shall grant you
a merciful death.

340
00:23:38,046 --> 00:23:41,030
Dancing After School

341
00:23:36,770 --> 00:23:41,030
Next Time

